      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;â€œHey, Adora.â€ Catra smirks, her surprise only given away by the familiar twist of her eyebrows. She looks warm and out of place with the cluttered kitchen behind her. â€œDid you know Razz here makes the best pie?â€&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;â€œYou know what pie is?â€ That wasnâ€™t the right question to ask. She needs to know why Catra is here and if Razz is in danger, but itâ€™s the first thing that comes out.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Catra rolls her eyes. â€œThere was always contraband food around, Adora. You were the only one too high and mighty to try it. Stupid, considering youâ€™re always starving.â€ Adora stares in disbelief, losing focus as she watches Catraâ€™s black nails drum against the scuffed wood of Razzâ€™s counter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;â€œOh. I always wanted to give you the new things I tried.â€ Adora replies, trying to disguise the disappointment in her voice as she refocuses on Catraâ€™s face.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Catra narrows her eyes and scoffs. â€œYou shouldâ€™ve thought about that before you left.â€&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;OR&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Adora and Catra start running into each other at Madame Razz's cottage. For some reason, they both keep ending up back there again. Season 2 canon divergence.&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
